:["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: '...cannot resolve a public counterpart for the key it just signed under'","_opcert_signing.py:275-280 _opcert_own_public_keys returns pubs for every path in _opcert_own_key_paths, deduped — not indexed to the signing key path","_opcert_signing.py:241-258 _opcert_own_key_paths returns the multi-entry chain"],"finding":"AC1's contract is keyed to 'the key it just signed under,' but the named resolver _opcert_own_public_keys returns the deduped set of public lines for the ENTIRE ordered own-key chain (binding key, REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH override, genesis), not the pub for the specific signing-key path. A chain where a DIFFERENT key's pub resolves would make the aggregate non-empty even when the signing key's own public half cannot be derived, so the guard as specified can miss the exact key it claims to check.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbf4469a09783be2b","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 (MINT) / AC1","norm_id":"n4b29a0bd83436a6b","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A deployment whose binding key path resolves a pub but the genesis/override key (the one actually chosen by ensure_opcert_key for this mint) cannot: aggregate non-empty, AC1 silent"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","b